hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"291","We are Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, we are Ibn Aliya, we are Muhammad bin Ishaq. H Muhammad bin Aban told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Adi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Sa`id bin Ubaid bin al-Sabbaq told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Sahl bin Hunaif, he said: I was suffering from pre-mission due to severe and hardship, and I was bathing frequently due to it, so I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He excused himself from that and said: “Only ablution will reward you.” I said: So what if it gets on my clothes? He said: “It is sufficient for you to take a handful of water and sprinkle it on your garment where you see that it has fallen.” Ibn Aban said, he said: Saeed bin Ubaid bin Al-Sabbaq told me. Abu Bakr said: The hadith of Sahl bin Hunaif, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about pre-ejaculatory fluid. He said: “In it is ablution.” I said: Have you seen what It gets on our clothes? He said: “It is sufficient for you to take a handful of water and sprinkle it on your garment where you see that it has reached.” I dictated it before the chapters on madhiy."
